  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The current best is config_008 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) at 0.725 acc. All multiprofile variants with these encoders have been tested and none exceed it. The key unexplored dimension is whether the multiprofile + transformer aggregation step is actually necessary or whether a simpler singleprofile architecture with the same best encoders (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l) and best fusion (weighted) could match or exceed it. Config_031 is the direct singleprofile analog of config_008, removing the aggregation step while keeping all other optimal choices. This tests whether the ~2% gain from transformer aggregation over avgpool (0.725 vs 0.706) is truly additive or whether a cleaner single-profile pipeline avoids overfitting. It is also cheaper (no aggregation layer, estimated ~2–3 GPU hours vs 3.60 for config_008). If it matches or beats 0.725, we gain a cheaper alternative; if it underperforms, it confirms config_008 as the robust optimum and the final experiment can be used to verify or fine-tune around it. This is the highest-information, lowest-cost experiment available given the strong evidence already gathered."
}

